      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LAMBAY (8) tackled the Country Champs qualifiers before the break after holding his own in Open sprints prior. JVO reunites with him now having guided him to victory previously and he boasts a strong fresh effort. Looks well placed to land a blow on resumption. ATMOSPHERIC ROCK (3) was beaten twice here before winning at Forbes last start when rounding them up from the back. He's likely to get back again which is his downfall, but he's racing in good order and should be flying late in the race. RAVALLI (4) was in good touch prior to tackling midweek company last start at Canterbury. back to this grade is a big tick and he maps to get every chance. Can get back to winning ways. WHO BUT ROO (1) is better suited here and beat RAVALLI last time he lined up at this track and trip. Can bounce back with the aid of an inside barrier. MASTER OF DISGUISE (6) is first-up but has class and can't be discounted.",
